{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.matrixModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.matrixModel","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L65-L82","doc":"**De-axiomatisation (concrete model, bean `ovh1`).** The `n×n` real matrix\nalgebra with the **transpose** `σ = (·)ᵀ` and the matrix trace `τ` is a\ngenuine instance — every carrier axiom is a theorem, not an assumption:\nanti-multiplicativity is `Matrix.transpose_mul`, involutivity is\n`Matrix.transpose_transpose`, trace-invariance is `Matrix.trace_transpose`,\nthe Markov/cyclic law is `Matrix.trace_mul_comm`, and the identity matrix\nis `σ`-fixed (`Matrix.transpose_one`). So the spin-involution apparatus —\nhence the LP-dual invariance results proved over it — is realisable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.cost_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.cost_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L56-L63","doc":"**Step 3.** The cost functional `τ(c · x)` is `σ`-invariant:\n`τ(c · σx) = τ(c · x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_isometry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_isometry","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L50-L54","doc":"**Step 1.** `σ` is an isometry of the Frobenius pairing:\n`⟨σa, σb⟩ = ⟨a, b⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.pairing","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L47-L48","doc":"The Frobenius pairing `⟨a,b⟩ = τ(ab)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_c","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L41-L41","doc":"`σ` fixes the cost: `σ(c) = c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.c","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The LP cost element `c`, fixed by `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.tau_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.tau_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Cyclic / Markov property `τ(ab) = τ(ba)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.trace_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.trace_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Trace-invariance `τ ∘ σ = τ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L33-L33","doc":"`σ` is involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_antimul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.sigma_antimul","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Anti-multiplicativity: `σ(a)·σ(b) = σ(b·a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.σ","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L29-L29","doc":"The spin involution `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.τ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.τ","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L27-L27","doc":"The Markov trace `τ : A → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance","kind":"structure","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance.lean#L19-L41","doc":"The spin-involution / Frobenius-trace apparatus.\n\nA `definition` carrier: a ring `A`, the Markov trace `τ`, the spin\ninvolution `σ`, and its structural properties — anti-multiplicativity\n`σ(a)σ(b) = σ(ba)`, involutivity `σ∘σ = id`, trace-invariance `τ∘σ = τ`,\nthe cyclic (Markov) property `τ(ab) = τ(ba)`, and a `σ`-fixed cost `c`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance","label":"prop:spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}